Initialize compiler-visible scratch before conditional writes.

Applies to picotls f06553b877ada93c860dd1db9002eabf7365292d.
GCC Release builds cannot prove that every live curve word is initialized
before use, or that the cipher-selection assertion succeeded before its
output is inspected. Keep assertions and warnings enabled; initialize the
scratch arrays and test output explicitly instead of suppressing diagnostics.
The corresponding micro-ecc arrays remain unchanged in upstream as audited
on 2026-10-13. No algorithm, curve geometry, or selection policy changes.

